Z||000000||fierohuddy||05-24-2001||10:19 PM||||Can anyone tell me the difference between a 1986 v6 se and a 1985 v6 gt?  Both cars in question are 4 spd||||reg||5
Z||000001||Oreif||05-24-2001||10:34 PM||||Gages above radio pod, Third brake light, Subwoofer (if equipped) rear speakers in sail panels, SE had same style seats as fastback GT's (emblem and stripe), Sail panel windows say "SE", lower ground effects are painted black, and 4-spoke steering wheel with Paddle horn buttons are all on the 86 SE.<P>The 85 GT had seat speakers, no 3rd brake light, No premium sound option (Sub) GT has 3-spoke steering wheel with GT crest. Lighter grey interior. Seats were usually light gray center dark gray sides (on gray interior). sail windows marked "GT", ground effects painted silver, and all gages in the dash.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">    <BR><B><I>Got Emblems?</I></B>||||reg||1
Z||000002||rockcrawl||05-25-2001||08:27 AM||||The '86 SE will have backlit gauges, '85 GT does not.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Monkeyman||05-25-2001||10:05 AM||||If both are basically identical cars (mileage, condition, price, options), I'd buy the '86SE.  (This is from someone who currently drives an '85 GT and just sold another '85 GT.)<P>MM||||reg||1
Z||000004||RossT||05-25-2001||01:42 PM||||Monkey, Why do you say that??||||reg||1
